[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I\'ll teach you how to use Joy AI image edit. It can change clothes. It can move objects. It can rotate the camera. It can combine multiple reference images. And it can also output changing the face or the original scene.'

[00:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And I\'ll show you how to fix the cropping problem. In Joy AI image edit, you will find two main models. The first model is Joy AI image edit which lets you edit a single'

[00:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'image and another one is Joy AI image edit plus used for multiple image edits. If your computer has low VRAM there is an INT8 compressed version of this model'

[00:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and this version is very useful for 30 series graphic cards and it also works great on 40 series and 50 series cards. In my testing, this INT8 version is'

[00:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'faster than the FP8 version and it\'s also less compressed. Right now, there is no smaller official version, distilled model or lura available. And just because of this, you'

[01:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'must download the full model file. You also need the coin 3 VL8B text encoder. An int8 compressed version of this text encoder is also available to'

[01:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'save your memory. For the VAE, we will use the old VEN 2.1 VA model file. To set everything up, first update your'

[01:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Confi and restart it. After the update, you will find the required Joy AI nodes in your menu and you will see the text encode joy image'

[01:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'edit node for single image editing and the joy AI image edit plus and also used for multiple image editing. So first we\'ll focus on single image'

[01:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'editing. The plus model can sometimes work with only one image. However, the developers created two separate models for different tasks. It\'s much better to use the correct'

[02:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'model for each task to get the best results. For this workflow, I am using the following settings. Steps 30, CFG4, uler sampler, scheduleuler, normal, and'

[02:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a den noiseise value of one. In my testing, these settings work very well for me. Now, let\'s test our very first edit. So'

[02:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'here I loaded an image and wrote a very simple prompt. Change the color of the dress on the walking women from pale blush pink to deep emerald green. So first I tested the image at different'

[02:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'resolutions. And when I did this the results in the four image grid didn\'t look good. Some of the results were cropped some were zoomed in and the edits were not'

[03:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'consistent. So after running multiple tests I found a solution. The longer side of your input image should never be more than,024 pixels. And to fix this I'

[03:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'resized the longer side to,024. And this gave me a vertical image with a resolution of 768 by,024. Now you can see that the model'

[03:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'successfully changed the dress color to deep emerald green. The face didn\'t change and the color edit looks excellent. However, I noticed that the model still cropped of part of the image. When the'

[03:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'image is processed by the text and code joy image edit node, the final result can look slightly zoomed or cropped. And to understand this cropping issue better, I tested different den noiseise'

[03:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'values. At a den noiseise setting of 0.7, the result wasn\'t good. But crop problems were solved. So when I increased the d noiseise value to one, I'

[04:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'got a much better edit, but the image was still cropped. Next, I tested a square image with a resolution of,024 by,024 pixels. Using a square image fixed the cropping'

[04:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'problem and the best part of this model is how well it preserves the face of your subject. The body, pose, background, lighting and other details also remained completely consistent.'

[04:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'This model is indeed very useful for clean image editing. To completely solve the cropping problem with vertical images, I used a resize and pad node. Use the resize and pad'

[04:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'node to place that image inside a square,024x,024 canvas. Because your original image is vertical, this node adds wide padding on the left'

[05:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and right sides. Now you can send the complete vertical image into the Joy AI model without cropping the top or bottom of your composition.'

[05:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'After the model finishes your generating the image, simply crop out the white padding on the sides. This returns your final edited image to its original 768 by,024 vertical size while keeping your'

[05:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'full composition and keeping the face consistent. Next, I gave the model a more difficult task with two changes in a single'

